  "worked_solution": "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n-(x-1)(x+5)\\ge 0,\n$$\n\nis a \"*greater than or equal to*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=-(x-1)(x+5)\n$$\n\nis *above* the $x$-axis or *touches* this axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/f4b9cd7557301e663b226e155bef4603d552b1c866411bc687ab4a082efeeaf5.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $-5\\le x\\le 1.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
